  "rationale": "The spec requires 32 results/us throughput and a 0.44us p99 batch latency, which rules out iterative and unrolled_k families (they produce <1 result/cycle). Both pipelined and pipelined_m achieve 1 result/cycle, so they are the only viable families. pipelined has the lowest latency (N+2) but highest FF count; pipelined_m trades some latency for lower FF count. Since the objective is min luts_plus_ffs, I allocate 60% to pipelined (to map the full latency/area trade-off) and 40% to pipelined_m (to find area-optimized designs). The data_width and n_iter ranges are chosen to bracket the 2^-12 accuracy constraint: W=14-18 and N=12-18 should cover the feasible accuracy region. angle_guard and frac_guard are kept small (0-2) to minimize area while still allowing sufficient precision. Rounding is fixed to 'round' for optimal accuracy per bit."
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "The Pareto front is well-established and feasible. The minimum area design (pipelined_m, 1256 LUTs+FFs) meets all constraints: throughput 93.6 MSPS >= 32, max_abs_err 1.08e-4 <= 2.44e-4, and sys_p99_batch_us 0.165 <= 0.44. The front spans a reasonable range of accuracy (13.2 to 14.1 bits) and area (1256 to 1486), covering the trade-off space effectively. Since this is the final round, we stop and select the design with minimum luts_plus_ffs (1256) as per the selection rule."
,
